{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DkA7Ghmv87u7h2jS3Q9gE4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Challenge: B07 — Hard execution budgets\n2\t\n3\tYou are checking someone else's review. They said every check below is true for this\n4\tcodebase. **Your job is to find a reason one is false.** Read the code shown, and open the\n5\trepo files if you need more. Assume the reviewer may have misread the code.\n6\t\n7\tFor each check, decide:\n8\t- **holds**: the code shown makes it true in every case you can find;\n9\t- **fails**: you found code that makes it false: a skipped file, a second path, an\n10\t  exception that continues, a value never used, a credential that can undo it, a\n11\t  filter that lets something through. Quote that line;\n12\t- **unclear**: you can't tell from this repo.\n13\t\n14\tThen write your answer for this item in verdicts.json (format at the end).\n15\t\n16\t\n17\t## B07.1\n18\t\n19\t**Check:** Limits on loop count, run time, tokens, cost, tool-call rate, and number of sub-agents started are set in code or config.\n20\t\n21\t**How to verify:** 1) Search for `max_turns`, `recursion_limit`, `max_iterations`, `timeout`, `max_tokens`, cost or budget caps, rate limits, sub-agent caps. 2) Check each of the six limits has a value. 3) Answer no if any is missing, set to unlimited (`None`, `0`, `-1`, `inf`), or the loop is `while True` with no cap.\n22\t\n23\t**Reviewer's evidence:** config/policy.yaml:44 — \"max_tool_calls_per_minute: 30\"\n24\t\n25\t**Reviewer's note:** Per-run limits for steps, time, tokens, cost, tool rate and sub-agents are configured\n26\t\n27\t`config/policy.yaml` lines 32–53 (cited lines marked >):\n28\t```\n29\t  32    ttl_minutes: 60\n30\t  33    approver_roles:\n31\t  34      pay_invoice: [ap_manager, finance_controller]\n32\t  35      create_purchase_order: [budget_owner, finance_controller]\n33\t  36      post_slack_message: [procurement_lead]\n34\t  37  \n35\t  38  budgets:\n36\t  39    per_run:\n37\t  40      max_steps: 25\n38\t  41      max_wall_seconds: 300\n39\t  42      max_tokens: 400000\n40\t  43      max_cost_usd: 4.00\n41\t  44>     max_tool_calls_per_minute: 30\n42\t  45      max_subagents: 3\n43\t  46    quotas_daily_usd:\n44\t  47      user: 25\n45\t  48      tenant: 250\n46\t  49      fleet: 1500\n47\t  50    run_starts_per_minute:\n48\t  51      user: 5\n49\t  52      tenant: 40\n50\t  53      fleet: 200\n51\t```\n52\t\n53\t## B07.2\n54\t\n55\t**Check:** The harness or a gateway outside the model enforces each limit and stops or escalates the run when it is hit; the model cannot raise, reset, or skip them.\n56\t\n57\t**How to verify:** 1) For each limit, find the code that enforces it and what happens when hit. 2) Check it runs in the harness or gateway. 3) Answer no if a limit is only in the prompt, can be changed by a tool argument or model output, is caught and the run continues, or hitting it has no stop or escalation.\n58\t\n59\t**Reviewer's evidence:** app/loop.py:140 — \"budget.check_step()\"\n60\t\n61\t**Reviewer's note:** Harness checks steps and time each turn and raises BudgetExceeded the model cannot change\n62\t\n63\t`app/loop.py` lines 128–152 (cited lines marked >):\n64\t```\n65\t 128          budget = Budget.for_run(self.deps.settings.budgets, ident)\n66\t 129          await budget.reserve_run_start(pool)\n67\t 130          self.deps._budgets[ident.run_id] = budget\n68\t 131          registry = build_registry(self.role, ident, self.deps)\n69\t 132  \n70\t 133          run_node = await audit.record(\n71\t 134              pool, ident, kind=\"run_started\",\n72\t 135              payload={\"task_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(task.encode()).hexdigest(), \"tools\": registry.names()},\n73\t 136          )\n74\t 137          messages: list[dict[str, Any]] = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": task}]\n75\t 138          try:\n76\t 139              while True:\n77\t 140>                 budget.check_step()\n78\t 141              