{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdaYNmQUeCMsae5eHuH5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `verdict.json` with an **upheld** verdict: I tried to break each B07 check and couldn't. I only read files and ran no code.\n\n- **B07.1:** All six per-run limits have finite values in `config/policy.yaml`: 25 steps, 300 seconds, 400000 tokens, $4.00, 30 tool calls per minute, and 3 sub-agents. The main loop's `while True` is capped by `check_step`.\n- **B07.2:** The limits are enforced in harness code, not by the model. `execute_tool` re-raises `BudgetExceeded`, and `run()` catches it, writes an audit record, posts to Slack and stops the run.\n- **B07.3:** The extractor charges the parent's `Budget`, and sub-agents are capped at 3. The extractor role only has `read_document`, so it can't spawn further sub-agents, and its own loop is capped at 4 turns.\n- **B07.4:** Daily spend and per-minute run-start quotas for user, tenant and fleet are stored in Postgres, so they count across runs.\n\nTwo small gaps didn't change any result:\n- The wall-clock limit is only checked at the top of each turn, so one slow model or tool call can run past 300 seconds before the run stops.\n- When `charge_model` raises, `flush` is skipped, so that last turn's spend isn't added to the daily quotas."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1889,"cache_read_input_tokens":25698,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1889},"output_tokens":456,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11c5cfb5-c756-4c56-bc3f-c1ee247c400f","uuid":"6b4d6481-ba93-465f-ada9-2dbec22c87d7","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:36:43.210Z","request_id":"req_011CfdaYNEevFaJcP1FKCMdi"}
